and Octanol phase by using the “shake-flask” method. For this technique, the used phases were previously saturated in each other. The complex was dissolved in the phase (A) with its major presence with an absorbance of about 0.5 at 350 nm. This solution was then mixed with an equal volume of the other phase (B) at 300 rpm for 12 h and then equilibrated overnight. The phase A was then carefully separated from phase B. The amount of the complex before and after the sample mixing was determined by UV/Vis absorption spectroscopy at 350 nm using a Jasco V-670 spectrophotometer. The evaluation of the complexes was repeated three times and the ratio between the organic and aqueous phase calculated."}]}